        rec("How does blockchain work?", "**Blockchain** = Distributed, immutable ledger.\n\n```\nBlock 1          Block 2          Block 3\n[Data]    →     [Data]    →     [Data]\n[Hash: abc]     [Hash: def]     [Hash: ghi]\n[Prev: 000]     [Prev: abc]     [Prev: def]\n```\n\n**Key properties:**\n1. **Decentralized**: No single authority (thousands of nodes)\n2. **Immutable**: Can't change past blocks (hash chain breaks)\n3. **Transparent**: Anyone can verify transactions\n4. **Consensus**: Nodes agree on valid state (PoW, PoS)\n\n**Use cases:** Cryptocurrency (Bitcoin), smart contracts (Ethereum), supply chain tracking, digital identity.\n\n**Limitation:** Slow (Bitcoin: ~7 tx/sec vs Visa: ~65,000 tx/sec), energy consumption (PoW).", "english_general"),
